  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1225 AM CDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nCooler & Cloudier Start to New Week:\n\nWhile upper level GOES water vapor imagery loops depict three upper \nlevel areas of cyclonic rotation along and west of the Mississippi \nRiver Valley, the local forecast area will remain mostly unaffected \nand dry through the start of the week due to temporary amplification \nof the residual upper level ridge. The upper level low over southern \nCanada seen shifting east estranges a surface frontal boundary, \ncurrently bifurcating the western half of the forecast area, into a \nlow level stretching axis through Sunday. As a result, an area of \nlow level anticyclonic rotation over southwest Canada temporarily \nstrengthens the synoptic ridging over the forecast area through \nSunday, shunting the subsequent upper level low currently over the \nDesert Southwest farther northwest than previously forecasted Monday \nnight through Tuesday. Resultant precipitation potential (20-40%) \ngrazes locally western counties in southeast Minnesota overnight \nthrough Monday night. May not see any measurable precipitation out \nof this round as synoptic forcing is weakening and ridging affects \nlocal forecast area. \n\nA cloudier and cooler forecast than recent days is expected due to \nthe passing synoptic lows and a filament of increased low level \nmoisture over the forecast area. \n\nLow Confidence In Precipitation Through The Week:\n\nEventually, the upper level low slowly sagging south along the \nPacific Northwest on upper level GOES satellite imagery loops grabs \nthe leftovers of the early week upper level low with potentially a \nmore zonal orientation towards the forecast area through the late \nweek. Although, a similar low level anticyclonic setup could abstain \nthe local forecast area from the higher precipitation potential \ncurrently suggested by the NBM (40-60%) until next weekend when the \nGEFS (24.12Z) advects a mid level trough through the central CONUS. \nAlthough, the concurrent EPS (24.12Z) suggests mid level ridging \nwith diffluent flow at the time which will affect the widespread 50-\n75% PoPs initialized in most recent NBM for Day 7.",
